 MF=1, GENERAL INFORMATION                                        9543 1451  417
  MT=451, COMMENTS AND DICTIONARY                                 9543 1451  418
  MT=452, TOTAL NUMBER OF NEUTRONS PER FISSION                    9543 1451  419
    IT IS THE SUM OF DELAY NEUTRONS (MT=455) AND PROMPT           9543 1451  420
    NEUTRONS PER FISSION (MT=456).                                9543 1451  421
  MT=455, T.R.ENGLAND +,LA-11151,LA-11534,LAURA-88-4118           9543 1451  422
 MF=2, MT=151, RESONANCE PARAMETERS                               9543 1451  423
  RESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETERS FOR SLBW FORMULA IN 1.0E-5 TO     9543 1451  424
  1.5E+2 EV RESONANCE ENERGY REGION                               9543 1451  425
   RESOLVED PARAMETERS  WERE RECOMMENDED AS FOLLOWING:            9543 1451  426
   IT WAS NOTICED THAT THE PARAMETERS OF THE FIRST SEVERAL WELL   9543 1451  427
   DEFINED RESONANCES (0.308, 0,576, 1.276, 1.928, 2.372, 2.358   9543 1451  428
   EV, FOR EXAMPLE) GIVEN BY DERRIEN ET AL.  5| (TRANSMISSION),   9543 1451  429
   KALEBIN ET AL. 6| (TRANSMISSION) AS WELL AS WESTON ET AL.  7|  9543 1451  430
   (ABSORPTION, NOMALIZED TO THERMAL CAPTURE CROSS SECTION OF 582 9543 1451  431
   B) RESPECTIVELY ARE IN EXCELLENT AGREEMENT WITH EACH OTHER.    9543 1451  432
   THIS FACT MEANS THAT THE RESONANCE PARAMETERS FOR THE FULL     9543 1451  433
   RESONANCE ENERGY REGION CAN BE COMBINED BY AVERAGING WEIGHTED  9543 1451  434
   WITH RANDOM ERROR ONLY WITHOUT TAKING THE 8% SYSTEMATIC ERROR  9543 1451  435
   IN ABSORPTION MEASUREMENT  7| INTO ACCOUNT. SO THAT THE        9543 1451  436
   RECOMMENDED VALUES FOR MOST RESONANCES WERE AVERAGED IN EQUAL  9543 1451  437
   WEIGHT EXCEPT THOSE FOR WHICH THE RANDOM ERRORS OF WESTON ET   9543 1451  438
   AL.'S MEASUREMENT OR/AND THE ERRORS OF KALEBIN ET AL.'S        9543 1451  439
   MEASUREMENT ARE MUCH LARGER THAN DERRIEN ET AL.'S, IN SUCH     9543 1451  440
   CASES THE AVERAGE WERE MADE WITH UNEQUAL WEIGHTS PROPERLY.     9543 1451  441
  UNRESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETERS IN 1.5E+2 EV TO 30 KEV ENERGY   9543 1451  442
  REGION                                                          9543 1451  443
   KIKUCH'S PARAMETERS  4| WERE USED AS INPUT DATA AND ADJUSTED   9543 1451  444
   TO FIT THE CAPTURE CROSS SECTIONS (EVALUATED ON THE BASES OF   9543 1451  445
   WESTON ET AL.'S, VANPRAET ET AL.'S  8|, WISSHAK ET AL.'S  9|   9543 1451  446
   AND DERRIEN ET AL.'S MEASUREMENTS) AND FISSION CROSS SECTION   9543 1451  447
   OF DABBS  10| (AVERAGED IN PROPER ENERGY RANGE) THEN THE       9543 1451  448
   RECOMMENDED UNRESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETERS WERE OBTAINED.     9543 1451  449
